From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Joseph Telaak <joseph@telaak.dev>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 17:32:17 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] drm/bridge: adv7511: Accept S32_LE I2S samples

Commit 7c3127e4814c ("drm: bridge: adv7511: remove s32 format from i2s
capabilities") dropped S32_LE because hw_params rejected it.

Some I2S controllers can only send a sample that fills its slot, so with
32-bit slots S32_LE is the only format they can offer. Accept it as a
24-bit sample: the ADV7511 takes the top 24 bits of the slot, hdmi-codec
already reports 24 significant bits, and the IEC958 channel status
already treats 32-bit samples as 24-bit.
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/bridge/adv7511/adv7511_audio.c | 4 +---
 drivers/gpu/drm/bridge/adv7511/adv7511_drv.c   | 1 +
 2 files changed, 2 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/bridge/adv7511/adv7511_audio.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/bridge/adv7511/adv7511_audio.c
index 87e7e820810a..474834a94f7c 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/bridge/adv7511/adv7511_audio.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/bridge/adv7511/adv7511_audio.c
@@ -105,9 +105,7 @@ int adv7511_hdmi_audio_prepare(struct drm_bridge *bridge,
 		len = ADV7511_I2S_SAMPLE_LEN_20;
 		break;
 	case 32:
-		if (fmt->bit_fmt != SNDRV_PCM_FORMAT_IEC958_SUBFRAME_LE)
-			return -EINVAL;
-		fallthrough;
+		/* S32_LE: the top 24 bits of the slot, as for IEC958 */
 	case 24:
 		len = ADV7511_I2S_SAMPLE_LEN_24;
 		break;
diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/bridge/adv7511/adv7511_drv.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/bridge/adv7511/adv7511_drv.c
index d3964adbb106..0cff81a6c086 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/bridge/adv7511/adv7511_drv.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/bridge/adv7511/adv7511_drv.c
@@ -1351,6 +1351,7 @@ static int adv7511_probe(struct i2c_client *i2c)
 						  SNDRV_PCM_FMTBIT_S20_3LE |
 						  SNDRV_PCM_FMTBIT_S24_3LE |
 						  SNDRV_PCM_FMTBIT_S24_LE |
+						  SNDRV_PCM_FMTBIT_S32_LE |
 						  SNDRV_PCM_FMTBIT_IEC958_SUBFRAME_LE),
 	adv7511->bridge.hdmi_audio_spdif_playback = 1;
 	adv7511->bridge.hdmi_audio_dai_port = 2;
